<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19497" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gergŏvĭa</span></b> , ae,
			f.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A town of the Arverni</i>, <i>in
				Aquitanian Gaul</i>, perh. in the neighborhood of the modern
				<i>Clermont</i>, now 
			<i>Jargean</i>, <i><span class="en">Caes. B. G. 7, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">34</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">36</span></i>; 44.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A town of the Boii</i>, <i>to the east
				of the Liger</i>, perh. the mod. <i>Charlieu</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Caes. B.
				G. 7, 9 <i>fin.</i></span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>